Ladybird now resolves the margins of an in-flow grid item to its own
margins, with zero for an auto margin. Blink and Gecko report the same:
Blink’s MarginTop::CSSValueFromComputedStyleInternal() reads the
fragment’s margins (LayoutBox::MarginOutsets()), and its grid layout
places an aligned item by adding AlignmentOffset() to its grid area’s
offset, keeping auto margins at zero. Gecko’s nsComputedDOMStyle::
GetMarginFor() returns a length as it is, and the used margin
otherwise, which stays zero for an auto margin of a grid item, since
nsGridContainerFrame aligns items with a separate offset in
AlignJustifySelf(). WebKit also positions an aligned grid item with a
separate offset, in RenderGrid::columnAxisOffsetForGridItem(). But
its GridLayoutFunctions::updateAutoMarginsInRowAxisIfNeeded() writes
the space that auto margins absorb into the item’s margins, which its
computed style then reports, so it reports nonzero auto margins.
